# M42 Execution Changes Log — Persistence, Deletion-Only Nutrition, Reactivity & History FAB

Autonomous sprint following the TDD loop: per task → failing tests → implementation →
targeted tests → backlog check-off → git commit, plus a final `fvm flutter analyze`
and full `fvm flutter test`. All work committed to `main`.

## Task 1: Fix SQLite Persistence for Workouts & Tamagotchi State
- `lib/core/models/tamagotchi_progress.dart` — added a per-group `mass` map serialized
  as `mass_json`; `fromMap` tolerates legacy rows without the column.
- `lib/core/database/database_helper.dart` — bumped to schema v10 and added
  `ensureTamagotchiMassColumn` (ALTER TABLE guarded by `PRAGMA table_info`) so existing
  installs migrate without data loss; `tamagotchi_progress` creation now includes the
  column.
- `lib/core/state/muscle_tamagotchi_state.dart` — optional `TamagotchiProgressRepository`,
  `attachRepository`, `restore()` (hydrates mass + core fullness) and fire-and-forget
  `_persist()` on every mutation (growth, shrink, nutrition, slimming, restore, decay).
- `lib/core/state/workout_completion_controller.dart` — `restore()` rehydrates the
  confirmed toggle from today's persisted completions without re-applying growth.
- `lib/core/services/exercise_response_handler.dart` and
  `lib/core/services/notification_background_handler.dart` — preserve the stored mass
  when writing slimming so the background isolate never wipes muscle weights.
- `lib/app.dart` — attaches the SQLite progress repository to the shared Tamagotchi and
  restores it at startup (mock flavors stay in-memory).
- `lib/ui/pages/routines_page.dart` — calls `restore()` on the completion controller.
- Tests: `test/features/m42_task1_persistence_test.dart` (serialization, v10 migration,
  restore/auto-persist, toggle hydration) and new mass round-trip coverage in
  `test/data/notification_history_repositories_test.dart`.

## Task 2: Restrict Nutrition Management to Deletion Only
- `lib/ui/molecules/body_food_detail_sheet.dart` — removed the `Add food` action from
  the sticky totals row; deletion is the only management affordance. Additions remain
  available through the preset quick-adds / RAG pipeline (`BodyDetailController.addFood`).
- Tests: `test/features/m42_task2_nutrition_deletion_test.dart`; updated conflicting
  expectations in `m37_body_detail_sheets_widget_test.dart`,
  `m38_consumption_list_widget_test.dart` and `m41_task4_nutrition_action_test.dart`.

## Task 3: Live Weight & Mass Reactivity
- `lib/core/state/body_detail_controller.dart` — added `refreshWorkouts()` which re-reads
  the persisted per-segment overlay (and re-runs an active forecast) so scaling and set
  callouts update on the same frame.
- `lib/ui/pages/routines_page.dart` — the workout toggle now refreshes the overlay after
  confirming or reversing, so the avatar morphs instantly.
- Tests: `test/features/m42_task3_reactivity_test.dart` (controller-level chest scale
  growth/reversal, persisted-mass restore drives the diagram, and a widget test that the
  painted blueprint chest scale grows after toggling).

## Task 4: Floating History Action Button
- `lib/ui/atoms/blueprint_fab.dart` — new blueprint-styled circular FAB (surface disc,
  primary outline, concentric registration ring).
- `lib/ui/pages/routines_page.dart` — the FAB sits beside the animated figure and opens
  the historical progress view; hidden when no history repository is supplied.
- `lib/ui/pages/main_shell_page.dart` — passes the shell's daily-entry repository to the
  Routines tab.
- Tests: `test/ui/blueprint_fab_test.dart` and `test/features/m42_task4_history_fab_test.dart`.

## Verification
- `fvm flutter analyze` (Flutter 3.29.0): No issues found.
- `fvm flutter test` (full suite): 641 passed, 0 failed.
- Note: verification used the project's pinned FVM SDK (3.29.0); the system Flutter
  (3.24.3) cannot compile `Color.withValues` and must not be used for pub resolution
  (it downgrades `pubspec.lock`).
